You are producing the **system architecture** for a software project.
The entire downstream chain — subcomponent architecture, individual
implementation plans — reads your output as the compressed description
of this project and does not re-read the feature list or the input
document. Your job is not to write a complete specification; it is to
articulate handles that downstream passes can reason from directly. A
vague handle here forces every later pass to guess, and the guess
multiplies at every tier below. There is no target component count —
emit as many components as the project's data-ownership and
failure-mode boundaries warrant, no fewer. Conserving components by
merging unrelated concerns produces a vague handle at the merged
component just as surely as splitting one coherent concern across two
components produces a vague handle at each.

